 ## Compatibility Decisions Made in This Release
 
-### 1. Promoted Rails 7.2 (`7.2.4`) to `Gemfile` on `config.load_defaults 7.2` and Moved to Ruby `3.4.8`
-- Updated `.ruby-version` from `3.2.9` to `3.4.8` and tightened the Ruby
-  constraint in `Gemfile` and `Gemfile.next` to `ruby '>= 3.4.0', '< 3.5.0'`.
-- Promoted `rails` `7.2.4` (and `activerecord-sqlserver-adapter ~> 7.2.0`) from
-  `Gemfile.next` into `Gemfile` / `Gemfile.lock`.
-- Updated shared gem constraints for Ruby 3.4 and Rails 7.2 / 8.1 dual-boot:
-  - `roadie-rails ~> 3.4.0` (`3.1.x` caps `railties < 8.0`; `3.4.0` supports
-    both Rails 7.2 and Rails 8.1).
-  - `sqlite3 >= 2.1` (required by ActiveRecord 8.0+; fully supported by Rails
-    7.2 and ships precompiled Ruby 3.4 binaries).
-  - `nokogiri ~> 1.19.5` (required by Rails 8.1.4.1 via `rails-html-sanitizer
-    >= 1.7.2` and `loofah >= 2.25.3`).
-  - Ruby 3.4 standard gems: updated `csv ~> 3.3.0`, `net-imap ~> 0.5.0`,
-    `net-smtp ~> 0.5.0`, and explicitly declared `benchmark` and `ostruct`
-    (required by `mini_magick` and `net-ldap`, silencing Ruby 3.4 default-gem
-    removal warnings).
-- Enabled `config.load_defaults 7.2` in `config/application.rb`, adopting Rails
-  7.1 and 7.2 defaults including:
-  - `active_support.message_serializer = :json_allow_marshal` and
-    `active_support.use_message_serializer_for_metadata = true`
-  - `active_support.cache_format_version = 7.1` and
-    `active_record.marshalling_format_version = 7.1`
-  - `active_record.default_column_serializer = nil`
-  - `active_record.run_commit_callbacks_on_first_saved_instances_in_transaction = false`
-  - `active_record.run_after_transaction_callbacks_in_order_defined = true`
-  - `dom_testing_default_html_version = :html5`
-  - `add_autoload_paths_to_load_path = false` and `yjit = true`
-- Removed the Rails 7.0-only `config.active_support.cache_format_version = 6.1`
-  override in `config/application.rb` (Rails 7.2 removed `6.1` as a write
-  format, and previous production Rails 7.0 already includes
-  `RedmineRails71CacheFormatRollbackCompat`).
-- Kept permanent app-compatibility override
-  `config.active_record.belongs_to_required_by_default = false` (Redmine
-  defines optional `belongs_to` associations without `optional: true`).
-- Resolved all `load_defaults 7.2` (7.1/7.2) application incompatibilities
-  directly so no extra framework-default overrides are needed:
-  - **`active_record.run_commit_callbacks_on_first_saved_instances_in_transaction = false`**:
-    in `app/models/issue.rb`, moving a child issue with subtasks across projects
-    saved the child, then saved its subtasks whose `recalculate_attributes_for`
-    reloaded and re-saved a second instance of the same child inside the same
-    transaction — replacing the commit-callback instance and dropping
-    `create_parent_issue_journal`. Fixed by scheduling
-    `create_parent_issue_journal(old_parent_id, new_parent_id)` from
-    `after_save` / `after_destroy` via `self.class.current_transaction.after_commit`.
-  - **`active_record.run_after_transaction_callbacks_in_order_defined = true`**:
-    in `app/models/issue.rb`, reordered `after_create_commit :add_auto_watcher`
-    ahead of `after_create_commit :send_notification` so auto-watched authors
-    continue to be added as watchers before creation notifications are sent.
-  - **`dom_testing_default_html_version = :html5`**:
-    updated `app/views/layouts/mailer.html.erb` (`<span class="header|footer">`
-    -> `<div class="header|footer">` and `span.footer` -> `.footer` for valid
-    HTML5 block nesting around formatted `<p>` elements) and updated
-    `test/unit/mailer_test.rb` (`'/p:nth-last-of-type(1)'` -> `'ul + p'` to
-    match HTML5 `DocumentFragment` semantics).
-- Fixed Ruby 3.4 and `sqlite3 >= 2.1` frozen / chilled string issues:
-  - `app/models/wiki_content_version.rb`: duplicated uncompressed `data`
-    (`data.dup`) before calling `force_encoding("UTF-8")` (avoids `FrozenError`
-    on frozen binary strings returned by `sqlite3 2.x`).
-  - `lib/redmine/i18n.rb`: duplicated strings (`dup.force_encoding("UTF-8")`)
-    to eliminate Ruby 3.4 chilled `Symbol#to_s` warnings.
-  - `app/views/gantts/show.html.erb`: used mutable `+"gantt_hdr"` literals to
-    eliminate Ruby 3.4 chilled string literal warnings.
-- Updated `config/environments/test.rb` (`config.action_dispatch.show_exceptions = :all`)
-  and migrated `config.cache_classes` -> `config.enable_reloading` in
-  `config/environments/{development,production,test}.rb`.
-- Retired Rails 7.0-only shims:
-  - `config/initializers/upgrade_rotations.rb`: removed the
-    `if Rails::VERSION::MAJOR == 7 && Rails::VERSION::MINOR == 0` block
-    (`RedmineRails72MessageVerifierRollbackCompat` and
-    `RedmineRails71CacheFormatRollbackCompat`).
-  - `config/initializers/10-patches.rb`: removed the Rails 7.0 `serialize`
-    kwargs shim, the `ActionView::Helpers::Tags::Base` fallback branch for
-    `add_options`, and the Rack 2 `Rack::RewindableInput#size` patch.
-  - `app/controllers/admin_controller.rb`, `lib/redmine/plugin.rb`, and
-    `config/initializers/30-redmine.rb`: removed Rails 7.0 `respond_to?`
-    fallbacks for `connection_pool.migration_context`,
-    `connection_pool.schema_migration`, `internal_metadata`, and
-    `Rails.application.deprecators`.
-
-### 2. Rollback Safety to Previous Production Rails 7.0 / Ruby 3.2.9 (N -> N-1)
-Verified live end-to-end between this release (Rails `7.2.4` on Ruby `3.4.8`)
-and previous production (Rails `7.0.10` on Ruby `3.2.9`):
-
-- **Session cookies (`_redmine_session`) & signed cookies (`cookies.signed`)**:
-  - Written as SHA256 PBKDF2 `aes-256-gcm` + `purpose: "cookie._redmine_session"`
-    + pure JSON payload (via temporary `cookies_serializer = :hybrid` override),
-    bit-for-bit identical to previous production Rails 7.0.
-  - Reads Rails 7.0 cookies natively, plus dormant Rails 6.1 SHA1 cookies and
-    pre-hybrid Marshal cookies via `upgrade_rotations.rb` and `:hybrid`.
+### 1. Promoted Rails 8.1 (`8.1.4.1`) into `Gemfile` and Removed `Gemfile.next` Dual-Boot
+- Promoted `rails` `8.1.4.1` and `activerecord-sqlserver-adapter ~> 8.1.0` from
+  `Gemfile.next` into `Gemfile`, and replaced `Gemfile.lock` with
+  `Gemfile.next.lock` (staying on Ruby `3.4.8`, `ruby '>= 3.4.0', '< 3.5.0'`).
+- Deleted `Gemfile.next` and `Gemfile.next.lock`.
